<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "demigirls" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Demigirls" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demiwomen" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demiwoman" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demigirl" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demilady" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demiladies" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demifemale people" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A gender identity describing someone who partially, but not fully, identifies as a woman or girl irrespective of their assigned gender. Used by cisgender, transgender, transfeminine, or nonbinary people who feel more strongly associated with women physically or socially, but not strongly enough to want to identify as one." .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigenderPeople> .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demigirls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://homosaurus.org/v2/cisgenderPeople> .
