<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demiguys" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demimen" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demimales" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demimale people" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Demiboy" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/demiboys> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A gender identity describing someone who partially, but not fully, identifies as a man or boy irrespective of their assigned gender. Used by cisgender, transgender, transmasculine, or nonbinary people who feel more strongly associated with men physically or socially, but not strongly enough to want to identify as one." .
