<https://homosaurus.org/v2/gymSubculture> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "gymSubculture" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/gymSubculture> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Gym subculture" .
<https://homosaurus.org/v2/gymSubculture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gay subculture popularized in the 1970s via homoerotic bodybuilder magazines. Often includes aesthetics modeled after ancient Greek gymnasiums. Especially popular in San Francisco, West Hollywood, and New York City." .
